        "crf": 16,
        "concurrency": 2,
        "art_direction": "A machine shop for numbers. Slate #161A26 ground, bone #F0EAD8 for all structure and all language, chartreuse #C9E265 marking whatever is measurably true, magenta #E5487B held for exactly one appearance at the turn. Fabricated data is drawn as hollow bone outline rather than given a hue. The signature device is a vernier caliper with a fixed beam and sliding jaws, which measures digit widths in sc07 and the span of a dataset in sc12-13 \u2014 the power and the limit as the same gesture. Motion is stepped or constant-rate everywhere except sc09, the single continuous move where the ruler stands up into the chart. Type is Space Grotesk 500/700 for language and Space Mono 400 for every measured number. Manim supplies every pixel of the picture; this Remotion layer is glass \u2014 the chip, the burned captions and two annotations, nothing else."
      },
